WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:07.420
Here's what I think canceling is and why
it's different from criticism.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:15.060
Criticism is expressing an argument or opinion with the idea of rationally influencing public opinion

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.580
through public persuasion, interpersonal persuasions.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:24.440
Canceling comes from the universe of propaganda, not critical discourse and it's about organizing

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:30.800
or manipulating a social environment or a media environment with a goal or predictable effect of isolating

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.300
or de-platforming or intimidating an ideological opponent.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.120
It's about making an idea or a person socially radioactive.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.160
Today you'll hear the activists say, well I didn't read the thing, I don't need to read the thing

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.840
to know that it's colonialist or racist.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.680
So an open society is a place that has a lot of intellectual pluralism,

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:58.260
a lot of diversity of viewpoints, it tries to pit bias and prejudice against other biases and prejudice

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:01.580
and it does that, by forcing contention and critical argument,

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.720
and forcing people to persuade each other overtime.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.560
That's really what science is.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:06.780
That's really what journalism is.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:12.000
The open society is not only incomparably better at producing knowledge than any other society

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.420
because it allows us to make errors and
not be punished for making errors,

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.340
it allows us to make errors in fact much more quickly.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.080
That's the secret of science. I call it liberal science.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:28.540
The magic of liberal sciences in the institutions that force us to channel these conversations

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.280
in socially productive ways.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:34.980
If you're an academic you're writing for journals you're undergoing peer review, you're being credentialed

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:38.140
by some kind of scientific organization.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:42.540
If you're a journalist you submit to ethics codes, you probably work for an organization

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.460
where you're supposed to tell the truth.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:50.140
All of these things are mediated in ways which allow us to be individuals but also to understand

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.420
some rules of engagement to follow each other.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:57.620
Society where you don't have that or community, like say twitter or like say

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:01.800
an academic culture where it's student to student and peer to peer, where you don't have

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:07.360
that kind of mediation going on, the social fabric turns into kind of lord of the flies,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:12.220
who can gang up on who. Who can make the most noise, who can attract the most followers,

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:15.880
and you begin to display to each other
instead of talking to each other.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:20.400
Weirdly, the way to help us be more
liberated as individuals is to

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.320
strengthen the institutions that we use
to connect each other.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.140
This is not a fight between one set of people and another set of people,

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.820
it is also a fight within ourselves.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.560
There are ideas that each of us hate

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.600
that it's very hard to restrain ourselves from not ganging up on in an illiberal way.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:41.180
The idea that wrong-headed and dangerous and heretical and blasphemous ideas should be not only

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:47.280
allowed but protected is preposterous, it's ridiculous, no society has ever had that idea—

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.553
until about 250 years ago.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:55.520
It shouldn't work but here we are and the reason is because despite its ridiculousness,

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:01.640
it has the one great advantage of being the single most successful social principle ever invented.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.680
 

